Patch 2025: memo for the per-draw fragment-program facts (size, code hash, sampled texture units).

Per draw the D3D12 path walked the fragment program three times: rsx_fp_texture_units, rsx_fp_program_size and rsx_fp_code_hash.
rsx_fp_info_memo() (rsx_fp_decompiler.c) answers all three from one entry per program: 4-way sets keyed on the hash of the first
instruction slot (not on the address: the game rewrites programs into a ring), each with a copy of the program bytes and a
per-slot skip mask. A slot is skipped in the comparison only when all three walks treat it as an inline-constant slot (the game
re-patches those each frame), so a hit means identical instruction slots and identical results. Programs longer than 1 KB or
without END are not memoised. Same idea as the v15 port's SHADER_HASH_MEMO, with a different key. SHADER_HASH_MEMO=0 runs the
three walks as before. Drawing thread only (not thread-safe). [PERF] shows "fpmemo hits/misses".

